# Local Python-function pilot implementation record — 2026-10-19

Continued the existing Workspace OS/Ruflo/Ollama inspection and Liam–Ada checkpoint `a4a1bce`. No discovery restart, reinstall, swarm activation or profile expansion. Scope was narrowed explicitly to a standalone Python function artifact workflow with independent user-supplied checks. This is not a general-purpose agent team.

Before editing, saved 15 selected source/profile originals in `pre-team-recovery.tar.gz` with a path/SHA256 manifest. Existing prototypes, archives and prior Git checkpoints were preserved. Added a local-only launcher branch, sequential persistent queue, restricted Python worker, direct installed Ruflo task-handler adapter, reviewer gate, handover evidence, restart/retry UI and named Desktop launcher. No source allowlist or Liam–Ada runtime change was required.

Reconciled the saved acceptance artifacts instead of rerunning successful work:

| Evidence directory | Observed result |
| --- | --- |
| `acceptance/initial-model-failure` | Candidate called `isdigit` on integers; real execution failed. No completion. |
| `acceptance/initial-format-failure` | Local response hit its token limit/malformed JSON. No execution/completion claim. |
| `acceptance/initial-intentional-contract-failure` | Model returned `print(1)` instead of the required function; rejected by executable contract. |
| `acceptance/review-drill-contract-failure` | First review drill also failed before review; not counted as a reviewer-rejection test. |
| `acceptance/success` | Actual Agents UI submission; sandbox produced 6, 0 and 3 for supplied inputs; Nora approved; Marguerite note and trusted handover saved. Final checkpoint `aa11268b7fe59b28fab138c5a1cd1988d2d54491`. |
| `acceptance/intentional-failure` | Valid function actually returned 6 with exit 0; independent expected value was deliberately 7. Execution gate blocked review/completion. |
